# Automerge API & modeling source of truth

For **any Automerge-related change** in this repo — CRDT document shape, `Automerge.change` / mutations, Repo wiring, IndexedDB / BroadcastChannel / WebSocket adapters, sync server, schema init / migration, counters / `Int` / `Uint` / `Float64`, rich text, or sync auth:

## Must

1. **Before coding**, fetch and consult the full Automerge LLM reference:
   - https://automerge.org/llms-full.txt
2. Prefer patterns documented there over training-data assumptions about Automerge / Automerge Repo APIs.
3. Align with repo design in `docs/architecture/offline-first-and-crdt.md` and budget model docs under `features/budgets/docs/`.
4. Prefer `@automerge/automerge/slim` (and Repo packages already in the tree) unless the official docs require a different entrypoint for the task.

## Must not

- Invent Automerge APIs, sync protocol details, or conflict-resolution behavior from memory alone.
- Skip `llms-full.txt` because a similar change was done earlier in the same session — re-check when the API surface or modeling guidance is in play.
- Treat blog posts or outdated cookbook pages as authoritative when they conflict with `llms-full.txt`.

**Canonical Automerge reference for agents:** https://automerge.org/llms-full.txt
